For a native domain, we need a login shell, that'd be provided by something called FacetLogin in /FacetOS/FacetLogin

This requires grabbing an IAuth object passed to the domain (which then passes it to the login process).

How IAuth works internally isn't nailed down yet - for now it'll allow any username other than root.

The user "root", password "facet" is obviously the typical root user - at least for now by default

IAuthService objects provide something like:
	authenticate(username, credential_type, credential_subtype, credential_blob, IPrincipal principal, IHumanUser user)
		principal is an out field identifying the principal via an IPrincipal object
		user is an out field for the IHumanUser

ISecurityManager is created by dominit, it's passed only to the login process
	It has a method
		CreateSession(IPrincipal p)

	That returns an ISession which is read-only, and gets passed to the shell
	ISession objects contain a read-only reference to the IPrincipal and have a method for spawning a new process

For a standard password login, credential_blob is just a string containing the password or password hash

credential_type is just an enum for now - and for now it contains only "Password"

credential_subtype is also an enum, but the intention is to have one enum for each type of credential blob

for now, just one for passwords, with different hash/PBKDF functions

IPrincipal has only getID() and getName() - it's intended for identifying ANY process, entity or agent that interacts with the system

System resources with permissions or ACLs etc name principals by ID

IPronouns
	Just a simple metadata object with get/set accessors for these fields, each field can be singular or plural
	Subject
	Object
	PossessiveDeterminer
	PossessivePronoun
	Reflexive
	ShortForm - this one does NOT take the agreement param

	enum IPronouns_GrammaticalNumber {
		PRONOUN_AGREEMENT_SINGULAR=1,
		PRONOUN_AGREEMENT_PLURAL=2,
	}

	example:
		IPronouns* gwen = ...
		gwen->SetSubject(PRONOUN_AGREEMENT_SINGULAR,"her");
		gwen->SetShortForm("she/her/hers");


IHumanUser has just metadata about an actual person as a user on the system
Some metadata is part of the actual interface definition, some is an arbitrary key/value store to allow extension without rewriting the ABI
Metadata part of the interface can be queried or updated via get/set accessors
	FullName     - make this a string of sane length
	Pronouns     - FacetOS is woke, oh no - make this an IPronouns
	HomePath     - make this a string for now
	DefaultShell - again, make this a string for now
	



